# LaTeX `\rowcolor` Command

The `\rowcolor` command is used to color entire rows in tables. It requires the **`colortbl`** package (or `xcolor` with the `table` option).

## Basic Setup

```latex
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}
% or
\usepackage{colortbl}
```

## Basic Syntax

```latex
\rowcolor{color}
```

## Examples

### Example 1: Simple Row Coloring

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}

\begin{document}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
\hline
\rowcolor{gray!30}
Header 1 & Header 2 & Header 3 \\
\hline
Data 1 & Data 2 & Data 3 \\
\hline
\rowcolor{blue!20}
Data 4 & Data 5 & Data 6 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{document}
```

### Example 2: Alternating Row Colors

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}

\begin{document}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
\hline
\rowcolor{lightgray}
Header 1 & Header 2 & Header 3 \\
\hline
\rowcolor{white}
Row 1 & Data & Data \\
\hline
\rowcolor{gray!20}
Row 2 & Data & Data \\
\hline
\rowcolor{white}
Row 3 & Data & Data \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{document}
```

### Example 3: Using `\rowcolors` for Automatic Alternation

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}

\begin{document}
\rowcolors{2}{gray!15}{white}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
\hline
Header 1 & Header 2 & Header 3 \\
\hline
Row 1 & Data & Data \\
\hline
Row 2 & Data & Data \\
\hline
Row 3 & Data & Data \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{document}
```

## Advanced Options

### Specify Column Range

```latex
\rowcolor{color}[left overhang][right overhang]
```

### Custom Colors

```latex
\definecolor{myblue}{RGB}{200,220,255}
\rowcolor{myblue}
```

## Tips

- Place `\rowcolor` at the **beginning** of the row (before the first cell)
- Works with `tabular`, `tabularx`, `longtable`, etc.
- Can be combined with `\cellcolor` and `\columncolor`

